# Fingerstyle Blues in E, steady thumb (repertoire plan: st-delta-blues-e). An original 12-bar
# country blues: E E E E | A A E E | B7 A E E. The thumb (p) plays steady quarter notes, lightly
# palm-muted, on one open bass string per chord: the open string 6 (E) in E bars, the open
# string 5 (A) in A bars, string 5 fret 2 (B) in the B7 bar. It never stops and never changes.
# The fingers (i on strings 3 and 2, m on string 1) play an E minor pentatonic melody in open
# position on strings 1-3, with slides: into string 1 fret 3 (G) from below, into string 2
# fret 3 (D) from below, and from the blue note, string 3 fret 3 (B flat), up to fret 4 (B).
# Swing: each beat is long-short, written as a triplet quarter (q3) then a triplet eighth (e3),
# so the melody's off-beat notes fall between thumb strokes.
# Ideas: bars 1 and 7 fall from G to B; the blue-note slide B flat-B and A-G answer it in bars 2,
# 4, 8 and 12; bar 6 climbs G A B D E against the A bass; bar 9 slides into D over B.
title: Fingerstyle Blues in E (steady thumb)
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original fingerstyle blues study
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 6
tags: blues, fingerstyle, country blues, monotonic bass, swing, slide, blue note
tempo: 84
time: 4/4
key: E

